-- Track M Day 2 (owner ruling): a collector job may end EMPTY_UNCONFIRMED. The
-- upstream answered with nothing, but its empty answers are unreliable (GDELT
-- DOC), so whether it holds anything is unconfirmed: never NOT_FOUND, never
-- zero. Generated by drizzle-kit from src/schema/enums.ts and
-- src/schema/work.ts. Expand only:
--   - EMPTY_UNCONFIRMED is appended to job_outcome (forward-only; nothing here
--     uses it as an enum value, which the transaction that adds it could not do);
--   - jobs_detail_only_not_found becomes jobs_detail_only_empty_answers: a job
--     keeps the detail of an unconfirmed empty answer as it keeps a not-found's,
--     compared as text for the same reason. Every existing row passes it: the
--     old check allowed a detail only with NOT_FOUND, and no row can hold the
--     new value yet. The application role already updates outcome_detail (0011).
ALTER TYPE "public"."job_outcome" ADD VALUE 'EMPTY_UNCONFIRMED';--> statement-breakpoint
ALTER TABLE "jobs" DROP CONSTRAINT "jobs_detail_only_not_found";--> statement-breakpoint
ALTER TABLE "jobs" ADD CONSTRAINT "jobs_detail_only_empty_answers" CHECK ("jobs"."outcome_detail" is null or "jobs"."outcome"::text in ('NOT_FOUND', 'EMPTY_UNCONFIRMED'));